  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>nnmf</keyword>
  <short_description>Nonnegative matrix factorization.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>[W, H] = nnmf(A, k)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>[W, H] = nnmf(A, k, Name, Value)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>[W, H, D] = nnmf(...)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <description>
    <p><b>nnmf</b> factors the nonnegative matrix A into nonnegative factors W and H so that W*H approximates A.</p>
    <p>Supported name-value options are Algorithm, W0, H0, Options, and Replicates. Algorithm can be als or mult. The Options structure can be created with statset and supports Display, MaxIter, TolFun, and TolX.</p>
    <p>The rows of H are normalized to unit length and columns of W are ordered by decreasing length. D is the root mean square residual.</p>
  </description>
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description />
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[A = rand(20, 10);
[W, H, D] = nnmf(A, 3)]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
